<p>Knowledge without action is worthless. Here is your step-by-step plan to implement everything in this guide over the next 30 days.</p>

<p>Week one, focus on foundations. Create your direct Google review link. Write your text message template. Train your team on the face-to-face ask script. Add review requests to your invoices. These high-impact strategies require minimal setup and deliver immediate results.</p>

<p>Week two, add automation. Set up your email drip sequence. Create review cards with QR codes. Launch your team incentive program. Choose and configure review generation software if your volume justifies it.</p>

<p>Week three, implement advanced strategies. Build your review funnel. Create video testimonial templates. Reach out to potential partners. Plan your first seasonal review campaign.</p>

<p>Week four, optimize and monitor. Track your review velocity. Respond to all existing reviews. Refine your scripts based on what is working. Set up reputation monitoring alerts.</p>

<p>By day 30, you should have a fully operational review generation system that runs whether you think about it or not. Your review count should be growing weekly. Your average rating should be stable or improving. And your local search visibility should be measurably better.</p>

<p>The contractors who win in local search are not luckier than their competitors. They are more systematic. They treat review generation as a core business process, not an afterthought. They ask every customer, follow up consistently, and handle negative feedback with professionalism.</p>

<p>You now have the exact strategies, scripts, and systems they use. The only question is whether you will implement them. Start today. Your next customer is already checking your reviews.</p>

